<title>USA: Toyota Motor to cut export volumes - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Toyota Motor to cut export volumes - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toyota Motor Corp, which increased exports in recent months amid robust U.S. orders and a strong U.S. dollar, plans to decrease export volumes rather than risk political consequences, the Wall Street Journal reported Friday.</p>
<p>The plan to scale back exports underscores rising tensions in Detroit, the newspaper reported.</p>
<p>Officials of the Big Three U.S. auto makers have complained the dollar's new strength makes their exports less competitive overseas.</p>
<p>The strong dollar has also given Toyota and other foreign competitors an advantage in the U.S. market, it said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
